---
title: Ciasto Pijak (Drunkard's Cake)
course: Dessert
locale: en
difficulty: Hard
cuisine: Polish
---

= Chocolate Sponge =

Preheat the oven to 180°C. Grease and line a #9″ by 9″ tin{}.

Make the chocolate sponge by placing the @eggs{3%large}(room temperature) and @sugar{75%g} in a bowl and beating over a pan of simmering water for ~{1%minute}, until the sugar has dissolved. Using a #handheld whisk{}, beat for about ~{3%minutes} until the mixture has tripled in volume.

Sift the @cocoa powder{2%tbsp}, @plain flour{35%g}, @cornflour{1%tbsp} and @salt{pinch} into the bowl, folding gently to just incorporate.

Spread the mixture in the tin and bake for about ~{12%minutes} until cooked. Remove and allow to cool for ~{10%minutes} before removing from the tin and leaving to cool completely.

= Poppyseed Sponge =

Prepare the poppyseed sponge using the same method, beating the @eggs{3%large}(room temperature) and @sugar{75%g} together before sifting in the dry ingredients (@plain flour{40%g}, @cornflour{1%tbsp}, @salt{pinch}, @poppyseeds{70%g}, and @flaked coconut{50%g}).

Bake for ~{12%minutes} or until done before cooling for ~{10%minutes} and removing from the tin.

= Creme Patisserie =

Put the @milk{425%ml} and @vanilla pod{1} in a #saucepan{} and bring to the boil. Take it off the heat and pour it into a bowl, allowing the vanilla pod to infuse the milk.

Mix together the @sugar{110%g} and @egg yolks{5} until the mixture is pale and thick. Remove the vanilla pod from the milk and discard. Slowly add the milk to the mixture, whisking constantly.

Add the @butter{10%g}, @plain flour{2%tbsp} and @cornflour{1%tbsp}, continuing to whisk the mixture. Return to the pan and bring to the boil, before reducing the heat and simmering the mixture for ~{3%minutes}, stirring continuously.

> Be careful; the creme patisserie burns easily, and quickly becomes too thick to spread easily.

Remove the mixture from the heat immediately and place into a bowl, covering with a sheet of greased baking parchment to prevent a skin from forming. Leave to cool completely.

= Assemble =

Place the chocolate sponge on the serving dish and spread the @cherry compote preserve{300%g}. Lay the poppyseed cake on top and spread the pastry cream. Place in the fridge to chill for at least ~{1%hour}.

Dip each @sponge (boudoir) fingers{1%pack} in @dark rum or vodka{250%ml} before placing them neatly in a single layer on top of the cake. Return to the fridge and chill for another ~{1%hour}.

Melt the @semi-sweet chocolate{200%g} and @vegetable oil{1%tsp} together and spread over the top of the cooled cake before sprinkling with the @walnuts{60%g}(chopped). Put back in the fridge overnight, and serve cold, cut into small squares.